          %h2#sec:orgcc9169c Definition
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/imaginary+element"} imaginary element
            of a (finitary)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+theory"} first-order theory
            is an equivalence class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X/E
            of a (finitary first-order)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definable+set"} definable set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            quotiented by a (finitary first-order)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definable+groupoid"} definable equivalence relation
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %strong hyperimaginary
            is an equivalence class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X/E
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definable+set#type-definable-set"}
              type-definable
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            quotiented by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definable+set#type-definable-set"} type-definable
            equivalence relation
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          %h2#sec:orgdc24af7 Examples
          %p
            The prototypical example of a hyperimaginary is an equivalence class of the quotient of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperreal+numbers"} hyperreal numbers
            by the equivalence relation “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            is infinitesimally close to
            = succeed "\u201D," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mrow
                          %mo |
                          %mi x
                          %mo −
                          %mi y
                          %mo |
                        %mi &lt;
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mi n
                        %mo )
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left( \left| x - y \right| &amp;lt; \frac{1}{n} \right)_{n \in \mathbb{N}}
          %h2#sec:org59c5525 Elimination of hyperimaginaries
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X/E
            be a hyperimaginary.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is said to
            %strong eliminate
            the hyperimaginary
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X/E
            (c.f.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elimination+of+imaginaries"} elimination of imaginaries
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X/E
            is interdefinable with a sequence of imaginaries, i.e. if every type-definable equivalence relation is, in fact, a conjunction of definable equivalence relations.
          %p
            %span.newWikiWord
              Stable theories
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/stable+theory"} ?
            eliminate
          %p hyperimaginaries. This is related to a result of Hrushovski’s that in a stable theory, (pro-definable) groupoids are pro-(definable groupoids).
          %h2#sec:org623f6fa Properties
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                In the same way that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Aut
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{Aut}(M)
                of a model acts on
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/imaginary+element"} imaginaries
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Aut
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{Aut}(M)
                acts on hyperimaginaries.
            %li
              %p
                Any hyperimaginary
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X/E
                in the sense of the previous paragraph can be extended to a quotient of the entire model
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi M
                        %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M^{\alpha}
                (in the (possibly infinitary)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} sort
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E'
                obtained by preserving
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                and extending it to be the discrete equivalence relation on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi M
                          %mi α
                        %mo \
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M^{\alpha} \backslash X
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                        %mo ′
                        %mover
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} df
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∧
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∨
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo =
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E' \overset{\operatorname{df}}{=} (E(x,y) \wedge (x,y) \in X \times X) \vee (x = y)
                = succeed "-invariant" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Aut
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝕄
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{Aut}(\mathbb{M})
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝕄
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{M}
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monster+model"} monster model
                have this form.)
            %li
              %p
                The process of taking points of hyperimaginaries in models (
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo ↦
                      %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M \mapsto M(X/E)
                ) does not commute with
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ultraproducts"} ultraproducts
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                is the equivalence relation in the reals of being infinitesimally close together, it’s easy to see that
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi 𝒰
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi E
                        %mo ¬
                        %mo ≃
                        %msup
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi E
                            %mo )
                          %mi 𝒰
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{\mathcal{U}}/E \not \simeq \left(\mathbb{R}/E \right)^{\mathcal{U}}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi E
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}/E \simeq \mathbb{R}
                (after all, the real numbers are Hausdorff) so that the right hand side is the nonstandard reals
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mo
                        %mo *
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ^* \mathbb{R}
                again (so every number has a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/halo"} cloud
                of infinitesimals around it) while the left hand side has no points which are infinitesimally close together.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              This is actually an excellent example of why we shouldn’t expect in general the process of taking points of hyperimaginaries in a model to commute with ultraproducts: on one hand, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              is a type-definable equivalence relation on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒰
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
              an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ultrafilter"} ultrafilter
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi 𝒰
                      %mo )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left(\prod_{i \in I} M_i/\mathcal{U} \right)(X/E)
              yields
              = succeed "-equivalence" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/germs"} germs
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi m
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi 𝒰
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [m_i]_{\mathcal{U}}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi φ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
